  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nThe 43rd & 52nd Light Infantry Chronicle 1892\n£40.00\n\nSorry, this item is out of stock\n\nA chronicle of events and news of the 43rd and & 52nd Light Infantry regiments from 1892, inlcuding maps, illustrations and historical articles. The 43rd & 52nd were predecessors to the Oxfordshire Light Infantry and later Oxfordshire & Buckinghamshire Light Infantry.\n\nCompiled and Edited by Captain A. F. Mockler-Ferryman\n\nPublished 1893 - Eyre and Spottiswoode, London\n\nHardback, 297 pages\n\nContents:\n\nRegimental Calendar for 1893\n\nDistinctions - VC., Distinguished Conduct Medal\n\nSir William Napier\n\nField Marshal Lord Seaton\n\nHumane Society's Medals\n\n43rd LI on Active Service\n\nHome and Foreign Stations of the 43rd LI\n\nHome and Foreign Stations of the 52 LI\n\nWar Services of the 52LI showing loses, &c\n\nThe 43rd Light Infantry in 1892\n\nThe 52nd Light Infantry in 1892\n\nExtracts from the London Gazette 1892\n\nLetters to the Editor from the 52nd Light Infantry\n\nArmy Signaling 1892\n\nMusketry 1892\n\nAthletics 1892\n\nFootball 1892\n\nCricket  1892\n\nMiscellaneous\n\n-The 43rd LI Dining Club\n\n-The Dinner in 1892\n\n- The 52nd LI Dinner\n\nThe Wreck of the Birkenhead\n\nWar Medals in the 43rdOfficers' Mess\n\nWar Medals in the 52nd Officers' Mess\n\nPictures in the 43rd LI Officers' Mess\n\nPictures in the 52nd Officers' Mess\n\nOld State of the 43rd  (1816)\n\nThe 43rd in 1864\n\nLast Indian Tour of the 43rd\n\nStates of the 52nd Light Infantry\n\nThe 2nd Battalion of the 43rd\n\nThe 2nd Battalion of the 52nd\n\nRifle Match in Malta 1871\n\nThe Winter March across the Portage of the Madawaska 1837\n\nThe Cholera Epidemic at Jhansi in 1862\n\nSport in the Andamans\n\nA Winter Trip to Norway\n\nWandering in Algeria\n\nMilitary Music\n\nOld Songs and Verses of the 43rd and 52nd\n\nGeneral Robert Crawford\n\nObituary Notice - General J. M. Primrose\n\nLate News - 52nd Football 1892\n\nNotice to Correspondents\n\nIllustrations\n\nMaps\n\n \n\nPlease Note: Original copies supplied, all in used but reasonable condition. Copy supplied may vary slightly from the one pictured in terms of wear and aging.\n\n \n\nRelated products\nIdentifying Cap Badges: A Family Historian’s Guide\n£25.00 Add to cart\nBugle & Sabre I\n£5.00 Add to cart\nThe Skipper’s War: Dragon School, Oxford & The Great War\n£20.00 Add to cart\nBugle & Sabre Magazine – Issue X\n£5.00 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
